CAT = "cehrsClinical"; SEG = "CLN"
Q = [
('A family practice wants every diabetes follow-up note to capture the same fields. What should the EHR specialist build?',
 'A diagnosis-based template', ['A new patient registration form', 'A separate chart for each visit', 'A free-text note with no fields'],
 'Clinical templates organized by diagnosis prompt for the same data each time, such as A1c, foot exam and eye exam, so documentation is complete and reportable.'),
('Which content belongs in a procedure template for a skin biopsy?',
 'Site, technique and specimen sent', ["The patient's insurance group number", "The provider's weekly schedule", "The clinic's supply order list"],
 'A procedure template captures what was done: the site, method, specimen and any complications, not billing or scheduling details.'),
('Why do clinical templates use drop-down lists for common findings?',
 'Coded data can be searched and reported', ['Drop-downs print in larger type', 'Lists stop providers from signing notes', 'They keep notes out of the legal record'],
 'Picking from defined values stores the data in a consistent, coded form, so it can be searched, counted and reported. Free text is harder to analyze.'),
('A pediatric practice builds a well-child template. Which field would it most likely include?',
 'Growth and developmental milestones', ["The parent's credit card number", "The pharmacy's opening hours", "The provider's license expiration"],
 'Well-child templates prompt for height, weight, head circumference, developmental milestones and immunizations due.'),
("A provider sends a new prescription from the EHR straight to the patient's pharmacy. What is this called?",
 'Electronic prescribing', ['Computerized order entry for labs', 'Remote patient monitoring', 'Interfaced charge capture'],
 'E-prescribing transmits prescriptions electronically from the EHR to the pharmacy, cutting errors from handwriting and phone calls.'),
('A clinic sends a referral packet to a specialist using a secure, encrypted email standard built for health care. What is this?',
 'Direct secure messaging', ['Regular office email', 'A text message to the specialist', 'A public file-sharing link'],
 'Direct messaging is an encrypted, standards-based way for providers to exchange health information, unlike ordinary email or texts.'),
('When patient data is sent over the internet to another provider, what protects it from being read in transit?',
 'Encryption', ['Compression', 'A cover letter', 'A read receipt'],
 'Encryption scrambles data so only an authorized recipient with the key can read it. Under the Security Rule, transmission security calls for it where reasonable.'),
('Which data on a clinic laptop most clearly needs to be encrypted?',
 'Stored electronic PHI', ["The vendor's user manual", "The clinic's public hours", 'A blank appointment template'],
 'Electronic PHI stored on devices, especially portable ones, should be encrypted so a lost device does not expose patients.'),
("A summary of a patient's problems, medications, allergies and results is sent to a new provider in a standard format. What is it?",
 'A continuity of care document', ['An explanation of benefits', 'A superbill for the visit', 'An accounts aging report'],
 'A continuity of care document (a C-CDA summary) packages key clinical data in a standard structure so another EHR can read it.'),
("A regional network lets hospitals and clinics in several systems look up each other's patient records. What is this?",
 'A health information exchange', ['A clearinghouse for claims', 'A practice management system', 'A local area network link'],
 'A health information exchange (HIE) moves clinical data among different organizations and EHRs.'),
('Under the national framework that links health information networks, what is a QHIN?',
 'A qualified health information network', ['A quality hospital improvement nurse', 'A quarterly health insurance notice', 'A qualified home infusion nurse'],
 'Under TEFCA, Qualified Health Information Networks are the connected networks that form a network of networks for nationwide exchange.'),
('Before sending records to a research team, what should be considered first?',
 'Its purpose and recipient', ['Which font the records use', 'How many pages will print', 'Whether the fax is in color'],
 'Purpose and audience decide what may be shared and how: research data may need authorization or de-identification, and only what the recipient needs should go.'),
("A nurse documents that the patient's left knee is swollen, but the same note later says right knee. What kind of error is this?",
 'A left and right mix-up', ['A misspelled patient name', 'Duplicate charting of a vital', 'A missing provider signature'],
 "Left and right mix-ups are common documentation errors that make the record unreliable and can lead to wrong-site care. They are corrected through the facility's amendment process."),
('A medical assistant enters the same blood pressure twice for one visit. What should be done?',
 'Correct the duplicate entry', ['Delete both readings', 'Average the two entries', 'Leave it, since both are true'],
 "Duplicate charting is corrected through the EHR's error-correction process, which keeps an audit trail. Deleting both loses the real reading."),
('During a peer review of notes, which problem should be flagged?',
 'An unsigned progress note', ['A note written in plain language', 'A note with a dated addendum', 'A note that lists the chief complaint'],
 'Reviews look for incomplete documentation, such as notes not signed or authenticated by the author.'),
('In SOAP notes, which section records the blood pressure the medical assistant measured?',
 'Objective', ['Subjective', 'Assessment', 'Plan'],
 'Measured findings such as vital signs and exam results go in the Objective section. Subjective is what the patient reports.'),
('In a SOAP note, where does the order for a follow-up visit in two weeks belong?',
 'Plan', ['Objective', 'Subjective', 'Assessment'],
 'The Plan records next steps: orders, prescriptions, education and follow-up.'),
('SOAPIER adds three sections to SOAP. What does the I stand for?',
 'Implementation', ['Interpretation', 'Inspection', 'Identification'],
 'SOAPIER is Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan, Implementation, Evaluation and Reassessing (as the NHA test plan expands it): it tracks what was done and how the patient responded.'),
('In SOAPIER charting, which section records how the patient responded to the care given?',
 'Evaluation', ['Implementation', 'Objective', 'Plan'],
 'Evaluation documents the result of the interventions, such as pain dropping from 7 to 3 after medication.'),
('In a problem-oriented medical record, how are progress notes organized?',
 'By each numbered problem', ["By the provider's schedule", 'By the payer to be billed', "By the clinic's room number"],
 'A POMR is built on a numbered problem list, and each progress note is written against the problem it addresses.'),
('A provider wants every diagnosis on a claim supported in the note. Which charting requirement does this reflect?',
 'Every diagnosis treated is charted', ['Notes kept under one page', 'Diagnoses written only on paper', 'Only the main problem charted'],
 'Charting must document the primary diagnosis and any secondary ones treated, so the record supports the codes billed.'),
('A chart opens with a red banner warning of a latex allergy. What type of EHR feature is this?',
 'A patient alert', ['A billing hold', 'A scheduling block', 'A portal notice'],
 'Patient alerts flag safety information, such as allergies or fall risk, whenever the chart is opened.'),
('An EHR flags that a 52-year-old patient is overdue for colorectal cancer screening. What is this flag tracking?',
 'A preventive care indicator', ['A late payment on the account', 'An expired insurance card', 'A missed portal login attempt'],
 'Health maintenance reminders and quality indicators flag care gaps such as overdue screenings, which also feed quality reports.'),
('During the visit, which data is entered in real time by the clinical staff?',
 'Vitals and the chief complaint', ["The patient's lifetime claim history", "The payer's contract rates", "Last year's audit results"],
 'Vitals, the reason for the visit and the exam are recorded as the visit happens, so the provider sees current data.'),
('A new patient brings a paper list of past surgeries. Where should they be documented?',
 'In the surgical history', ["In today's vital signs", 'In the billing notes', 'In the appointment comments'],
 'Historic data such as past surgeries, medications, immunizations and allergies is entered in the history sections of the chart.'),
("A new patient's immunization record from another state is entered. Which detail is most important to capture for each vaccine?",
 'The vaccine and the date given', ["The color of the vial's cap", 'The price of the vaccine', 'The name of the receptionist'],
 'An immunization history needs at least the vaccine and date given (and, when known, dose, lot and site) so the provider knows what is due.'),
('A patient says she has no known drug allergies. How should this be recorded?',
 'As NKDA in the allergy section', ['By leaving the allergy section blank', "In the plan of today's note only", 'As a free-text portal message'],
 'Recording "no known drug allergies" shows the question was asked. A blank list could mean no one asked.'),
('At a visit, the medical assistant reviews every drug the patient takes against the EHR list. What is this process?',
 'Medication reconciliation', ['Charge reconciliation', 'Claim adjudication review', 'Prior authorization'],
 "Medication reconciliation compares the patient's actual drugs with the record to catch omissions, duplicates and interactions at every care transition."),
('Who may enter a medication order through computerized provider order entry?',
 'A licensed prescriber', ['Any staff with an EHR login', 'The patient through the portal', 'The billing office on request'],
 'CPOE orders are entered by licensed providers, or by credentialed staff only where law and facility policy allow. An EHR specialist supports the system but does not place orders.'),
("A provider asks the EHR specialist to help find the order set for a chest pain workup. What is the specialist's role?",
 'Show her where to find it', ['Place the orders for her', 'Choose the tests she needs', 'Sign the orders as a witness'],
 'Supporting CPOE means helping users navigate and use the tools. Choosing and entering the orders stays with the provider.'),
('Why do CPOE systems lower medication errors compared with handwritten orders?',
 'No handwriting to misread', ['Orders skip pharmacist review', 'Doses are rounded up', 'Orders go out without a signature'],
 'Typed, structured orders cannot be misread and can be checked for allergies and interactions as they are entered.'),
('A provider wants a printed handout on wound care for a patient. Where should the EHR specialist look?',
 'The patient education library', ["The clinic's insurance contracts", 'The help desk ticket log', 'The scanner settings'],
 'Many EHRs include a searchable patient education library with handouts on topics such as wound care, smoking cessation and prenatal care.'),
('A patient asks the EHR specialist whether she should stop her blood pressure pill. What should be done?',
 'Pass it to her provider', ['Tell her to stop if she feels well', 'Print a side effects handout', 'Look up the dose and advise her'],
 "Clinical advice is outside the EHR specialist's scope, so the question goes to the provider or nurse."),
('Which search term would best find a smoking cessation handout in the education library?',
 'Quit smoking', ['Tobacco tax', 'Lung scan bill', 'Nicotine order'],
 'Education libraries are searched by plain-language topic terms. Billing or order terms will not return patient handouts.'),
('A nurse needs the lot number of a flu vaccine given last month. Where in the chart is it recorded?',
 'The immunization record', ['The problem list', 'The demographics screen', 'The insurance tab of the chart'],
 'Lot number, manufacturer, site and date are recorded with each dose in the immunization record.'),
("A provider wants to see how a patient's blood glucose readings have changed over a year. Which EHR view helps most?",
 'A flowsheet or trend graph', ['The face sheet summary', 'The appointment history', 'The referral list'],
 'Flowsheets and trend graphs show repeated measurements such as glucose, weight or blood pressure over time.'),
("Where would today's pulse and temperature be found in most EHRs?",
 'The vital signs section', ['The medication list', 'The surgical history', 'The guarantor information screen'],
 'Vitals are recorded in their own vital signs section, often shown on the visit summary and trend views.'),
('Which list shows the drugs a patient is currently taking?',
 'The medication list', ['The problem list', 'The order history', 'The encounter history list'],
 'The current medication list shows active drugs, doses and directions. Order history shows everything ever ordered.'),
('A patient joins a video visit from home. What should staff confirm at the start?',
 'Her identity and her location', ['Her credit score and employer', 'The make of her computer', "The time zone of the clinic's vendor"],
 "Telehealth workflows confirm the patient's identity and physical location (which matters for licensing and emergencies), along with consent where required."),
('Which step is part of preparing a patient for a scheduled telehealth visit?',
 'Sending a link and testing connection', ['Printing a paper chart for the patient', 'Booking an exam room for the visit', 'Mailing the patient a thermometer'],
 'Telehealth preparation includes sending the visit link and helping the patient test audio and video before the visit.'),
('A provider dictates a note after the visit, a day late. How should the entry show it?',
 'As a late entry, dated today', ['Back-dated to the visit day', 'As a new visit on that day', 'Without any date'],
 'A late entry is labeled as such and dated when it was actually written, while referring to the visit it describes. Back-dating misrepresents the record.'),
("Why should copy-forward of an old exam into today's note be avoided?",
 'Old findings may be out of date', ['It uses too much disk space', 'It hides the visit from billing', "It breaks the provider's login"],
 'Carried-forward text can document findings that were not examined today, which is inaccurate and may misstate the care given.'),
("A specialist wants a patient's last three lab results. What should be sent?",
 'Only the requested results', ['The whole chart since birth', "The patient's billing history", 'Every note from every provider'],
 'Sharing for treatment still follows the request: send what was asked for and needed, using a secure method.'),
('Which data class must certified EHRs be able to exchange under the national core data standard?',
 'Allergies and intolerances', ['Staff vacation schedules', 'Vendor contract prices', 'Parking lot assignments by unit'],
 'The United States Core Data for Interoperability (USCDI) lists the data classes for exchange, including allergies and intolerances, medications, problems, vital signs and immunizations.'),
("Lab results arrive from the hospital lab automatically and land in the provider's inbox. What links the two systems?",
 'An interface', ['A fax machine', 'A paper requisition', 'A shared password'],
 'An interface lets two systems, such as a lab system and an EHR, send data to each other automatically using standards.'),
('A provider orders a lipid panel, but no result arrives after two weeks. Which EHR feature helps catch this?',
 'An open order tracking list', ['The fee schedule', "The patient's portal password", 'The scanned insurance card'],
 'Order tracking shows orders that are still open or overdue, so missing results are followed up.'),
('An EHR specialist stands beside a provider during go-live to answer questions as she charts. What is this support called?',
 'At-the-elbow support', ['Tier three escalation', 'Off-site hosting', 'Batch processing'],
 'At-the-elbow support means helping users at their workstation in real time, common during go-lives and upgrades.'),
('A nurse at a distant clinic cannot find where to sign a note. What kind of point-of-care support fits best?',
 'Remote screen sharing help', ['A new computer delivered next week', 'A printed annual report', 'A message to the patient'],
 "Remote support lets the specialist see the user's screen and guide her through the step while she works."),
("Which document records a surgeon's description of a procedure, findings and specimens?",
 'Operative report', ['History and physical', 'Discharge summary', 'Consent form'],
 "The operative report describes the surgery performed, what was found, specimens removed and the patient's condition."),
("A banner in a patient's chart notes that a signed do-not-resuscitate order is on file. What kind of information does it flag?",
 'An advance directive', ['A billing hold', 'A payer denial', 'A portal lockout'],
 "Patient alerts can flag advance directives such as DNR orders, so care teams see the patient's wishes whenever the chart is opened."),
("A lab result is far outside the normal range. Which EHR feature brings it to the provider's attention?",
 'A critical value flag', ['A billing modifier', 'A scheduling rule', 'A portal reminder message'],
 "Abnormal and critical results are flagged so the provider sees them quickly; acting on them is the provider's decision."),
('Which procedure is performed by a health care professional rather than recorded as historic data?',
 "Today's injection in the office", ['A tonsillectomy at age eight', 'A vaccine given ten years ago', 'A past appendectomy'],
 'Procedures done during the visit are documented as they happen. Past procedures from before are entered as history.'),
("Which practice best protects a note's accuracy when it is corrected?",
 'Keep the original in the history', ['Overwrite the entry completely', 'Delete it and start over', 'Ask the patient to edit it'],
 'EHRs keep the original entry and show who changed it and when; the record must show what was there before the correction.'),
("A provider wants to open a patient's chart to the most recent echocardiogram. Where are imaging reports usually filed?",
 'Under results or imaging', ['Under demographics', 'Under appointments', 'Under payments and balances'],
 'Imaging and diagnostic reports are filed with results, often in an imaging or diagnostics tab.'),
('A hospice nurse asks which template to use for a home visit note. What should guide the choice?',
 'The visit type and its fields', ['The longest template in the system', 'The template the billing office likes', 'Whichever template opens first'],
 'Templates are chosen by visit type, so the note captures what that kind of encounter requires.'),
('A dermatology practice adds a template for acne follow-ups. What is one common use of such templates?',
 'Faster, consistent documentation', ['Longer visit times for patients', 'Fewer fields for quality data', 'Automatic approval of the claims'],
 'Templates speed charting and keep it consistent, which also helps quality reporting.'),
("A parent asks for her child's immunization record for school. Which source gives the official list?",
 'The EHR immunization record', ["The child's appointment list", "The family's billing statement", 'A note from the waiting room'],
 "The immunization record lists each dose given, so it is the source for school forms, released under the practice's policy."),
('Which data element is usually captured in real time when a vaccine is given?',
 'Lot number and injection site', ["The patient's employer name", 'The insurance claim number', "The clinic's tax ID number"],
 'Vaccine administration documentation includes the vaccine, dose, lot number, site, route and the person who gave it.'),
("A provider asks for all of a patient's A1c results in one place. What should the EHR specialist show her?",
 'The lab results trend view', ['The appointment calendar', 'The referral work queue', 'The guarantor record'],
 "Lab trend views list a test's results over time so changes are easy to see."),
("A patient's note lists 'Smith, Jon' but the chart says 'John Smith'. What should happen?",
 'Correct the name per policy', ['Leave it, since it is close', 'Delete the whole note', 'Open a new chart for Jon'],
 'Misspelled names are documentation errors that can lead to misidentification, so they are corrected through the proper process.'),
]
